    "['mpls l2vc [parameter1] [parameter2] tunnel-policy [parameter3]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols l2circuit neighbor 3.3.3.9 interface ge-1/0/0.1 virtual-circuit-id 101', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated Juniper equivalent command for the Huawei MPLS L2VC configuration:\\n\\n##\\nset protocols l2circuit neighbor 3.3.3.9 interface ge-1/0/0.1 virtual-circuit-id 101\\nset protocols l2circuit neighbor 3.3.3.9 interface ge-1/0/0.1 tunnel-policy policy1\\n##\\n\\nNote: While this is the direct equivalent, Juniper's implementation differs slightly in architecture:\\n1. The interface is specified at the neighbor level rather than being part of the VC command\\n2. Tunnel policies are applied separately in Juniper (though the same policy name is maintained)\\n3. The QoS parameters would need separate configuration under class-of-service settings\\n\\nThe VC ID (101) and neighbor address (3.3.3.9) remain the same as in the Huawei configuration.\", 'trans_template': 'set protocols l2circuit neighbor 3.3.3.9 interface ge-1/0/0.1 virtual-circuit-id 101'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols l2circuit neighbor 3.3.3.9 interface ge-1/0/0.1 tunnel-policy policy1', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated Juniper equivalent command for the Huawei MPLS L2VC configuration:\\n\\n##\\nset protocols l2circuit neighbor 3.3.3.9 interface ge-1/0/0.1 virtual-circuit-id 101\\nset protocols l2circuit neighbor 3.3.3.9 interface ge-1/0/0.1 tunnel-policy policy1\\n##\\n\\nNote: While this is the direct equivalent, Juniper's implementation differs slightly in architecture:\\n1. The interface is specified at the neighbor level rather than being part of the VC command\\n2. Tunnel policies are applied separately in Juniper (though the same policy name is maintained)\\n3. The QoS parameters would need separate configuration under class-of-service settings\\n\\nThe VC ID (101) and neighbor address (3.3.3.9) remain the same as in the Huawei configuration.\", 'trans_template': 'set protocols l2circuit neighbor 3.3.3.9 interface ge-1/0/0.1 tunnel-policy policy1'}]]": 1,
