    "['mpls te tunnel-id [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols mpls label-switched-path Tunnel10-to-3.3.3.9 tunnel-id 101', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the Juniper equivalent of the Huawei `mpls te tunnel-id 101` command:\\n\\n##\\nset protocols mpls label-switched-path Tunnel10-to-3.3.3.9 tunnel-id 101\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- In Juniper, MPLS TE tunnels are configured as label-switched paths (LSPs)\\n- The command creates/sets the tunnel ID for an LSP named \"Tunnel10-to-3.3.3.9\" (assuming this naming convention based on the Huawei interface Tunnel10 with destination 3.3.3.9)\\n- The tunnel ID 101 is preserved from the original configuration\\n- This would be part of the LSP configuration for the TE tunnel', 'trans_template': 'set protocols mpls label-switched-path Tunnel10-to-3.3.3.9 tunnel-id 101'}]]": 1,
    "['ospf [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [0, 0], 'trans_command': 'unit [parameter2] family inet service input [parameter3]', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]'}]]": 1,
