    "['mpls-te enable', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols ospf area 0.0.0.0 mpls-te', 'parent_command': ['set protocols ospf area [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set protocols ospf area [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nset protocols ospf area 0.0.0.0 mpls-te\\n##', 'trans_template': 'set protocols ospf area 0.0.0.0 mpls-te'}]]": 1,
    "['tunnel-policy [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols mpls tunnel-policy policy1', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set protocols mpls tunnel-policy policy1', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nset protocols mpls tunnel-policy policy1\\n##\\n\\nAlternatively, if you need the more detailed tunnel selection criteria equivalent to the Huawei \"tunnel select-seq te load-balance-number 1\" behavior, the Juniper equivalent would be:\\n##\\nset protocols mpls tunnel-policy policy1 then load-balance per-packet\\n##\\n\\nNote: The exact translation depends on Juniper device specifics. For true TE tunnel selection policies, Juniper typically uses path-computation configurations under `protocols mpls` or LSP definitions.', 'trans_template': 'set protocols mpls tunnel-policy policy1'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols mpls tunnel-policy policy1 then load-balance per-packet', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set protocols mpls tunnel-policy policy1 then load-balance per-packet', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nset protocols mpls tunnel-policy policy1\\n##\\n\\nAlternatively, if you need the more detailed tunnel selection criteria equivalent to the Huawei \"tunnel select-seq te load-balance-number 1\" behavior, the Juniper equivalent would be:\\n##\\nset protocols mpls tunnel-policy policy1 then load-balance per-packet\\n##\\n\\nNote: The exact translation depends on Juniper device specifics. For true TE tunnel selection policies, Juniper typically uses path-computation configurations under `protocols mpls` or LSP definitions.', 'trans_template': 'set protocols mpls tunnel-policy policy1 then load-balance per-packet'}]]": 1,
    "['tunnel select-seq [parameter1] load-balance-number [parameter2]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols mpls label-switched-path-load-balance te 1', 'parent_command': ['set protocols mpls tunnel-policy policy1'], 'root': 'set protocols mpls tunnel-policy policy1', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nset protocols mpls label-switched-path-load-balance te 1\\n##\\n\\nAlternatively, if you want a more precise translation that matches the tunnel selection sequence behavior:\\n\\n##\\nset policy-options policy-statement policy1 then load-balance per-packet\\n##\\n\\nNote: The exact translation depends on the specific Junos version and context. The first option directly translates the load-balancing aspect for TE LSPs. The second option creates a routing policy that enables per-packet load balancing, which is closer to the Huawei tunnel selection behavior.', 'trans_template': 'set protocols mpls label-switched-path-load-balance te 1'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set policy-options policy-statement policy1 then load-balance per-packet', 'parent_command': ['set protocols mpls tunnel-policy policy1'], 'root': 'set protocols mpls tunnel-policy policy1', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nset protocols mpls label-switched-path-load-balance te 1\\n##\\n\\nAlternatively, if you want a more precise translation that matches the tunnel selection sequence behavior:\\n\\n##\\nset policy-options policy-statement policy1 then load-balance per-packet\\n##\\n\\nNote: The exact translation depends on the specific Junos version and context. The first option directly translates the load-balancing aspect for TE LSPs. The second option creates a routing policy that enables per-packet load balancing, which is closer to the Huawei tunnel selection behavior.', 'trans_template': 'set policy-options policy-statement policy1 then load-balance per-packet'}]]": 1
